  I have been reading this newsgroup now for a month or two and have decided
I can now make some useful (?) comments myself.

  There have  been lots of people suggesting new weapons from various sources.
I think that some of these suggestions are quite warranted to,e.g. having
Mournblade as well as Stormbringer.I also like the suggestion of having
Grayswandir (btw has any more books in the Amber series after 'Sign of Chaos'
been released in the States?).However this has to be done carefully to avoid
tipping the scales to much in the player's favour,e.g. if you have read the
novel 'Stormbringer' you would know that someone possessing both Stormbringer
and Mournblade would be *very* powerful (the swords are controlled by the users
using verbal commands while not actually being held!).Maybe possessing both
blades could be made *extremely* difficult to counteract this.

  The suggestion of having Stormbringer randomly hit pets and peaceful monsters
is certainly well warranted,maybe this chance should increase with the frequency
of its use.One last thing on this topic,why doesn't Stormbringer have
regeneration properties? It certainly suggests this in the Elric books.

  If the development team do decide to have Grayswandir,then how about having
some trumps! You could have them for various places (altars,hell,the castle,etc)
as well as various creatures (the Wizard,Medusa,a creature to become your pet).
They could found as a pack of cards,and when applied a card is randomly selected
(until you know all the cards) and you may travel to the place or to where the
creature is.If the pack is cursed you get sent there whether you like it or not!

You gaze at the picture of the medusa -more-!

  We currently have here nethack 3.0 pl6 and I have notice that all the named
weapons appear as +0 weapons,which seems to contradict some the things people
have been writing about them,has this been changed by pl9?

  I have died in so many games lately by accidentally running in to floating
eyes lately that I may shoot myself if I do it again! Do other people do this
or is it just me? I *beg* the development team to have a message similar to that
for peaceful monsters,if this hasn't been done in pl7-9.

Do you really want to attack the floating eye ? [yn] uh,uh no way!

This has moved floating eyes very close to the top of my number-one-bad-guys-to-
genocide-at-the-earliest-possible-opportunity list! Yep ,they're right up there
with liches and rust monsters as my pet hates at the moment.
